# Mapbox Configuration
#
# PLACEHOLDER ONLY. This file is TRACKED. A real secret token sat on the line
# below until 2026-07-21, so it was in git history and on GitHub; it has been
# revoked. Put your real value in gradle.properties (gitignored) or export
# MAPBOX_DOWNLOADS_TOKEN in your environment.
#
# Issue at https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/ with exactly ONE scope:
#
#   DOWNLOADS:READ
#
# That is all it needs. It resolves the Mapbox SDK from Mapbox's private Maven
# repo at build time (android/settings.gradle.kts) and grants nothing at
# runtime.
#
# The RUNTIME token is a different, PUBLIC one (MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN) and never
# belongs in this file. Today it is used server-side by the Cloud Functions for
# search, geocoding and route optimization. It reaches the BROWSER once the live
# KinCare tracking map ships to kinfolk, so it should carry URL restrictions:
#
#   kinfolk.tribetails.com
#   auntie.tribetails.com
#   localhost
#
# Mapbox URL restrictions do NOT support wildcards, and they cannot be applied to
# an account's DEFAULT public token, so this has to be a purpose-made token with
# each origin listed exactly (100 max). Firebase preview channel URLs are
# generated per channel, so they cannot be pre-registered and the live map will
# not render in a preview. That is the accepted tradeoff; the KinTale route map
# avoids it entirely by being rendered server-side to a PNG.
MAPBOX_DOWNLOADS_TOKEN=sk.REPLACE_ME


# Other existing gradle properties...
org.gradle.jvmargs=-Xmx2048m -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
org.gradle.caching=true
android.useAndroidX=true
android.enableJetifier=true
